<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 23,577,000 bushels -- NOPA. [CORRECTED  13:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 23,577,000 bushels -- NOPA. [CORRECTED  13:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects title from 23,891,000 bushels to 23,577,000 bushels).</p>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association  weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity  in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 07/30/97    07/23/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 23,577,000  23,891,000    24,189,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  75,152	57,779	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    33,990,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting  only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding  by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by  state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   07/30/97    07/23/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,649,000   4,828,000     3,957,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 3,844,000   4,288,000     4,549,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,619,000   3,483,000     3,182,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,573,000   2,339,000     2,532,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  2,844,000   2,720,000     3,345,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,732,000   4,635,000     4,766,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,316,000   1,598,000     1,858,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	23,577,000  23,891,000    24,189,000</p>
</text>
